Built stdlib-only compress.py with the requested compression/decompression CLI. It uses mixed-radix packing for numeric records and base36 strings, binary packing for hex strings, and combinatorial encoding for line order, with bzip2 fallback for other inputs. The corpus compresses from 44,267 to 16,771 bytes—a 62.114% reduction, beating default zlib’s 22,390 bytes. Verified byte-identical restoration through the CLI and 105 additional round-trip tests. Registered python3 assay.py; repeated correctness checks run for at least 0.5 seconds, and the accepted assay reported 62.1140 with zero spread.